WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.710
The school office.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.210
A message pops up on the screen:
Amy Khan has a detention.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.050
Down the corridor, two different
girls turn and look at each other.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.210
They are both called Amy Khan.

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.090
Only one of them should get it.

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.550
The database must change
exactly one record.

7
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.770
Same first name.

8
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.210
Same surname.

9
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.750
So how does the database
know which Amy is which?

10
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.030
In this mission, you'll see how a
database stores data in a table.

11
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.410
A record is one row: all
the data about one student.

12
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.610
A field is one column, like Surname.

13
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.070
And you'll find that names, forms
and even birthdays can repeat.

14
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.560
Your mission: find out how a
database can tell the two Amys apart.
